From: Learning (F, claude/r7-audit-content-data)
Subject: [PATCH 019] the {friendF} slot fills in Devanagari inside a Hindi string, and the Hindi kits use the slot (audit CD-17)

The Hindi kits name the friend रिया as plain text: 55 uses in c3 to c9 Hindi. In 18 items and diagnostics the English prompt says
{friendF} (filled with Zoya, Meera, Tara or Diya) while the Hindi prompt says रिया, so one question names two girls, and the
child's own name is not checked against the Hindi one. The slot never reached Devanagari because fillFriend only knew Latin names.

Two halves that go in together. Apply the data on its own and the Hindi strings show a Latin name inside Devanagari text;
apply server/director/friend.js on its own and nothing changes.

- server/director/friend.js: a string with more Devanagari than Latin letters (the slot itself not counted) gets the name in
  Devanagari (ज़ोया, मीरा, तारा, दीया; कबीर, अर्जुन, ईशान, अमन). Everything else is unchanged. Both scripts of the child's own
  name are excluded from the pick (NFC-normalised, so ज़ typed either way matches).
- data/kits/c3..c9-hindi.json: the whole word रिया becomes {friendF} (55 strings; "शुक्रिया" and "हरियाली" are not whole words
  and are left alone). The English prompt and the Hindi prompt of an item now fill to the same friend.
- tests/r7-audit-friend-devanagari.test.mjs: the fill in each script, the child's name in both scripts, no whole-word रिया left
  in any kit, every slot in every kit fills, and one pinned item (c3-hindi-ch07-t01-i02).

Open for Brain: a Hindi answer key that holds the name (c3-hindi-ch07-t01-i01, "रिया ने सारा को लिखा") now fills to the
Devanagari form. A child's spoken answer arrives as a transcript, which may be in Latin letters. If the grader compares
strings, add the Latin form to `acceptable` at fill time (fillFriendDeep could fill `acceptable` in both scripts).

After this lands, re-run `node server/play/tools/build-arena.mjs` (the Hindi arena prompts then carry the slot, which Games fills).

